# Walking away from a conversation: the footer INTERRUPT closes its screen on the press, so the
# standing it costs was never shown anywhere. It is now put up as a result over the map, as an
# act's is, and kept on the tree with the one reply that was given.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period noon --observe-only "brewer"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# Reach the conversation through the verb that opens it.
strategy succeed
goal meet_stranger
advance 12 180
click observe "brewer"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "brewer"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
click act 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
wait mode Dialogue 60
advance 20 180

# One reply, then away before anything is settled.
click option 0
advance 20 180
click button
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# The result box: its own title, what was done, and — when the walking away cost standing — the chip.
expect INTERRUPTED
expect I walked away from
click continue
# The screen is read as drawn: a frame for the box to be gone from it.
wait
expect-not INTERRUPTED

expect-state trees dialogue with=brewer ending=interrupted replies=1
point dialogue last
wait
expect it came to: interrupted
expect "My name is Kenryc Greygate."
quit
